        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach_City%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "People from nearby areas originally built small summer houses and fishing camps along the shoreline of Beach City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach_City%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community was commonly known as Tri-City Beach and had about five hundred permanent residents by the early 1960s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach_City%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Beach City is now considered a part of the Greater Houston area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
